From 7c7edcb5cb26f30daf50a39a2bc5574aac41e27c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:14:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 067/240] Bugfix: size fixed vertex merging hash table
 according to number of fixed vertices [report R. Perry]

In `kgraphMapRbVfloMerge()`, the hash table was sized according to the
number of fixed vertex load slots, which is zero when all fixed vertices
have a zero load, while one slot is needed per distinct fixed terminal
domain. When these were more numerous than the table could hold, the
insertion loop never terminated. Size the table according to the number
of fixed vertices, bounded by the size of the target architecture, as
`kgraphMapRbVfloBuild()` does, and remove the now useless parameter.

Add a test case with zero-load fixed vertices on distinct terminal
domains.

Refs: GRA-01
---
 src/check/test_scotch_graph_map.c | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/libscotch/kgraph_map_rb.c     | 18 ++++++++---
 src/libscotch/kgraph_map_rb.h     |  6 ++--
 3 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/check/test_scotch_graph_map.c b/src/check/test_scotch_graph_map.c
index 04d38ae..572c397 100644
--- a/src/check/test_scotch_graph_map.c
+++ b/src/check/test_scotch_graph_map.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 /**   DATES      : # Version 6.0  : from : 12 aug 2014     **/
 /**                                 to   : 17 jul 2024     **/
